WEBVTT

00:32:59.895 --> 00:33:03.418
Do you want to maybe talk
about those in turn,

00:33:03.442 --> 00:33:04.665
of what that looks like,

00:33:04.689 --> 00:33:09.273
how would you build a mitigation strategy?

00:33:09.297 --> 00:33:11.623
I mean, first of all,
thinking about opportunity,

00:33:11.647 --> 00:33:13.781
how do you reduce
the number of opportunities

00:33:13.805 --> 00:33:15.072
to pass on the bug?

00:33:15.885 --> 00:33:17.643
AK: And so I think in that respect,

00:33:17.667 --> 00:33:21.328
it would be about massive changes
in our social interactions.

00:33:21.352 --> 00:33:23.877
And if you think in terms
of the reproduction number

00:33:23.901 --> 00:33:26.068
of being about two or three,

00:33:26.092 --> 00:33:27.473
to get that number below one,

00:33:27.497 --> 00:33:30.763
you've really got to cut
some aspect of that transmission